Hello, I'm Maneshwar. I'm building git-lrc, an AI code reviewer that runs on every commit. It is free, unlimited, and source-available on Github. Star Us to help devs discover the project. Do give it a try and share your feedback for improving the product.
In the previous discussion, we explored how PRAGMA gives you control over SQLite’s internal behavior. Now, let’s see how you actually structure smarter queries using subqueries and views. These aren’t just SQL features. They’re tools that help you write cleaner logic, reduce duplication, and make your database easier to work with. At its core, a basic SQL query looks like this: SELECT x FROM y WHERE z;
x → columns y → tables z → condition Now here’s where things get interesting: z (the condition) can itself contain another query. T…
